---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service · Bow Tie Kreative"
  description="Terms and conditions governing the use of Bow Tie Kreative's services and website bowtiekreative.com."
  canonical="https://bowtiekreative.com/terms"
>
  <section class="rp-section rp-backlight">
    <div class="rp-container">
      <div class="rp-legal">
        <span class="rp-eyebrow">Policies</span>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="rp-legal-date">Last updated: January 1, 2024</p>

        <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
        <p>These Terms of Service govern your use of Bow Tie Kreative's website and services. By using our site or services, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use our services.</p>

        <h2>2. Services</h2>
        <p>Bow Tie Kreative provides marketing, creative, strategy, and development services through a GrowthPoints system. The specific scope, deliverables, and terms of each engagement are outlined in a separate Service Agreement or Statement of Work.</p>

        <h2>3. GrowthPoints System</h2>
        <p>GrowthPoints are our proprietary capacity-based service model. Points represent value, complexity, effort, and production capacity — not time. Specific terms of point allocation, rollover, and job slots are defined in your Service Agreement.</p>

        <h2>4. Client Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>You agree to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate and complete information for service delivery.</li>
          <li>Respond promptly to requests for feedback, approvals, and materials.</li>
          <li>Pay all fees according to the agreed payment schedule.</li>
          <li>Not use our services for any unlawful purpose.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Payment Terms</h2>
        <p>Payments are processed via PayPal or other agreed payment methods. Fees are due as outlined in your Service Agreement. Late payments may result in service suspension.</p>

        <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>Upon full payment, we grant you ownership of the deliverables created specifically for your project. We retain the right to display completed work in our portfolio unless otherwise agreed.</p>
        <p>You retain ownership of all materials you provide to us. We grant no license to our methodologies, tools, or proprietary systems beyond the scope of the engagement.</p>

        <h2>7. Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>Both parties agree to keep confidential information shared during the engagement confidential, except as required by law or with prior written consent.</p>

        <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>Bow Tie Kreative's liability is limited to the fees paid for the specific service giving rise to the claim. We are not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including loss of revenue or business opportunity.</p>

        <h2>9. No Guarantee of Results</h2>
        <p>We do not guarantee specific business outcomes. Results depend on offer, market, budget, implementation, customer response, and client participation. We guarantee a transparent process, defined work, clear point values, and honest reporting.</p>

        <h2>10. Termination</h2>
        <p>Either party may terminate an engagement as outlined in the Service Agreement. Upon termination, fees for work completed are non-refundable. Unused prepaid points may be refunded or credited as agreed.</p>

        <h2>11. Website Use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use our site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of these terms.</li>
          <li>Attempt to disrupt, damage, or gain unauthorized access to our systems.</li>
          <li>Scrape, copy, or reproduce our content without permission.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>12. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>Our website and services may integrate with third-party platforms (PayPal, Google Analytics, etc.). These services have their own terms, and we are not responsible for their operation.</p>

        <h2>13. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Alberta and the federal laws of Canada applicable therein. Any disputes shall be resolved in the courts of Calgary, Alberta.</p>

        <h2>14. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms at any time. Changes are effective upon posting. Your continued use after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.</p>

        <h2>15. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these terms?<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:hello@bowtiekreative.com">hello@bowtiekreative.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .rp-legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .rp-legal h1 { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .rp-legal-date { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: var(--text-small); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .rp-legal h2 { margin-top: var(--space-7); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); font-size: var(--text-h3); }
  .rp-legal p { color: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .rp-legal ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-bottom: var(--space-5); }
  .rp-legal ul li { padding: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-2) var(--space-5); position: relative; color: var(--text-body); }
  .rp-legal ul li::before { content: '→'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--rp-accent); }
</style>